      "side": 1,
      "message": "`cdef_filter_8_{0,1,2}` and `cdef_filter_16_{0,1,2}` (lines 641-765) are split into 6 entry points specifically so `is_lowbd`, `enable_primary`, `enable_secondary`, and `clipping_required` constant-fold at compile time. Marking the shared 12-parameter `filter_block_4x4` `noinline` keeps the `block_width \u003d\u003d 8` prologues compact, but for 4:2:0 content every filtered chroma block has `block_width \u003d\u003d 4` (two calls per 8x8 luma CDEF block): without IPA constant-cloning, each call spills 6 of the 12 arguments to the stack on x86-64 and evaluates `is_lowbd`, `enable_primary`, `enable_secondary`, and `clipping_required` dynamically inside the loop. Was `noinline` measured on 4:2:0 chroma, or would per-variant `noinline` wrappers around an always-inline body (preserving constant folding while keeping `filter_block_4x4` out of the 8x8 fast path) work better?",
